gcc-14.2.0-libstdcxx-onyx.patch -- the one GCC source change of the aarch64-onyx-elf toolchain
(docs/POSIX-PLAN.md "WP-TC resolutions"; applied by tools/toolchain/build-onyx-toolchain.sh).

libstdc++'s configure, for a newlib target (--with-newlib), cannot link test programs (newlib
built without supplied syscalls: gcc_no_link) and so hard-codes what the target has:
 1. GLIBCXX_ENABLE_LIBSTDCXX_TIME: with =yes it runs link tests (fatal under gcc_no_link); with
    =auto it knows only named OSes. Onyx (*-onyx-*) is stated like the BSDs: clock_gettime with
    the monotonic and realtime clocks, nanosleep, sched_yield (all in libonyxposix)
    -> _GLIBCXX_USE_CLOCK_MONOTONIC, _GLIBCXX_USE_CLOCK_REALTIME, _GLIBCXX_USE_NANOSLEEP,
       _GLIBCXX_USE_SCHED_YIELD.
 2. The newlib block of configure.ac defines HAVE_TLS (and link, readlink, symlink, truncate,
    sleep, usleep, setenv, aligned_alloc, quick_exit, strerror_l, sockatmark) for RTEMS only:
    *-onyx-* takes the same list (newlib + libonyxposix provide every one)
    -> _GLIBCXX_HAVE_TLS (the exception globals per thread through __thread) and std::filesystem's
       hard links, symlinks, resize_file.
configure.ac and acinclude.m4 are patched with configure so the sources agree; configure is not
regenerated (no maintainer mode).

Copyright (c) 2026 Stéphane Wegener and the Onyx contributors. The patch itself: MIT licence (the
files it changes are GCC's, GPL-3.0-or-later with the GCC Runtime Library Exception).

--- a/libstdc++-v3/acinclude.m4
+++ b/libstdc++-v3/acinclude.m4
@@ -1762,6 +1762,19 @@
 
   if test x"$enable_libstdcxx_time" = x"auto"; then
 
+    case "${target}" in
+      *-onyx-*)
+        # Onyx (libonyxposix, docs/POSIX-PLAN.md WP-TC): clock_gettime with
+        # CLOCK_MONOTONIC and CLOCK_REALTIME, nanosleep and sched_yield.  The
+        # C library cannot be linked against at configure time (newlib
+        # without supplied syscalls: gcc_no_link), so state it as for the BSDs.
+        ac_has_clock_monotonic=yes
+        ac_has_clock_realtime=yes
+        ac_has_nanosleep=yes
+        ac_has_sched_yield=yes
+        ;;
+    esac
+
     case "${target_os}" in
       cygwin*)
         ac_has_nanosleep=yes
--- a/libstdc++-v3/configure
+++ b/libstdc++-v3/configure
@@ -21286,6 +21286,19 @@
 
   if test x"$enable_libstdcxx_time" = x"auto"; then
 
+    case "${target}" in
+      *-onyx-*)
+        # Onyx (libonyxposix, docs/POSIX-PLAN.md WP-TC): clock_gettime with
+        # CLOCK_MONOTONIC and CLOCK_REALTIME, nanosleep and sched_yield.  The
+        # C library cannot be linked against at configure time (newlib
+        # without supplied syscalls: gcc_no_link), so state it as for the BSDs.
+        ac_has_clock_monotonic=yes
+        ac_has_clock_realtime=yes
+        ac_has_nanosleep=yes
+        ac_has_sched_yield=yes
+        ;;
+    esac
+
     case "${target_os}" in
       cygwin*)
         ac_has_nanosleep=yes
@@ -28577,7 +28590,7 @@
 
 
     case "${target}" in
-      *-rtems*)
+      *-rtems* | *-onyx-*)
         case "${target}" in
           bfin* | lm32* | mips* | moxie* | or1k* | v850*)
             ;;
